(D5 - Discrepancy 5 repro: the --shared thing-crossing diagnostics locate their
 caret by scanning the SOURCE TEXT for the exported function's name and taking
 successive occurrences of it, rather than by the definition's own position. The
 comment below mentions the name once, so the first error - the parameter
 crossing - points at that comment, and the second error - the return crossing -
 takes the next occurrence and lands on the definition. Neither error is about
 the comment. This header deliberately does not spell the name, or the carets
 would move again.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox shared/D5.vox --shared -o libd5.so
 expected output:
   error: Exported function takes a point, which a library interface cannot
   describe yet - caret at D5.vox:19:27, inside the comment - then
   error: Exported function returns a point, which a library interface cannot
   describe yet - caret at D5.vox:24:5, the definition.
   No library is produced; this is a compile error.
